# R10: the Fated Tarot reading, the frame (the scene around the cards). Speakers adela_druskenvald, phillip_druskenvald.
# `reading draw` deals one upright Major Arcana to each of the four heroes from the playthrough seed (once; no repeats); `reading read hero_N
# adela_druskenvald` turns the card for slot hero_N (party order) and Adela speaks the card's verse from data/tarot/outcomes.json (drafted in
# tarot_outcomes.md). The module sets tarot_hero_1..4 (string flags holding the card id) and blesses each hero for an hour on `set tarot_full_reading`.
# Offered in the Lounge (from druskenvalds_lounge:ask_cards) and once more at the wreck (druskenvalds_wreck): a hero can put it off once.
# Drafted by Gemini (Gemini/sent_10_adela_reading.txt), edited; see README.md.

~ offer
if flag.tarot_full_reading
-> ask_again
endif
adela_druskenvald [smile]: Oh, sit down, all four of you, I can hardly stand it! You're simply glowing with a forecast, every last one of you.
adela_druskenvald [smile]: Just one card apiece, upright only, no funny business, I promise.
adela_druskenvald [sly]: Come on, darlings, let me have a peek! It'll do you a world of good before we get where we're going.
Narrator: She is already fanning the worn deck across the table, and reckon nobody here has agreed to a thing.
phillip_druskenvald [smile]: You may as well say yes, you know. She'll only ask again.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Best get it over with. Persistence like that outlasts mortar.
-> offer_menu

~ offer_menu
* Go on, deal the cards. -> shuffle
* What sort of reading is this? -> what_is_it
* [if not flag.gl_reading_deferred] Later. -> later
* [if not flag.gl_phillip_card_asked] Do you ever let her read yours, Phillip? -> phillip_card

~ what_is_it
adela_druskenvald [smile]: Twenty-two cards in the bundle, darlings, the Major ones, the ones with the faces on.
adela_druskenvald [neutral]: Each card tells where something meant for you is waiting out there in the dark.
adela_druskenvald [sly]: Fate leaves presents in the oddest places, you see, tucked under roots and behind old stones.
adela_druskenvald [smile]: I never know quite what the prize is, mind you, only that it is yours, near enough.
-> offer_menu

~ later
set gl_reading_deferred
adela_druskenvald [sad]: Oh, you're no fun at all when you're being sensible.
adela_druskenvald [smile]: Go on then, stretch your legs, but I'll ask again the moment you look bored!
phillip_druskenvald [smile]: Fair warning, my friends, she considers breathing a sign of boredom.
interject name:silas_vane: Lucky for the lady, I quit breathing years back.
-> ghostlight_express/druskenvalds_lounge:menu

~ phillip_card
set gl_phillip_card_asked
phillip_druskenvald [smile]: For me? My dear friends, a gentleman never peeks at his own hand before the betting is done.
phillip_druskenvald [sly]: Besides, I am already married to the finest fortune in the room.
phillip_druskenvald [neutral]: Leave the mysteries to the bold, I say, and pour another drink for the table.
adela_druskenvald [weary]: He's never let me. Not once.
adela_druskenvald [smile]: Calls himself a sport, and he won't even turn a single pasteboard for his wife!
interject name:cordelia_skein: Fascinating. A marriage held in stalemate by one unturned card.
Narrator: The silver goat on his cane catches the lamp, and the smile on his face does not move an inch.
-> offer_menu

# At the wreck, Adela insists (the reading is part of the council; there is no later).
~ at_the_wreck
adela_druskenvald [afraid]: Wait, wait just a minute, don't go marching off into the trees yet!
adela_druskenvald [neutral]: We never did turn your cards, and we have to do it now, while the moon is looking.
adela_druskenvald [smile]: Sit on that trunk, darlings, I won't take no for an answer out here.
phillip_druskenvald [weary]: Let her have it. We could all do with a little hope.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Hope's thin soup in a ditch like this, mister, but I reckon it warms the belly.
-> shuffle

~ shuffle
Narrator: The soft, cloth-edged cards whisper against her palms, and the rattle of the car seems to thin out and wait.
adela_druskenvald [smile]: Hush now, let the deck get your measure while I give them a proper mix.
adela_druskenvald [sly]: Close your eyes and think of nothing at all, or something, whichever you've got more of.
reading draw
-> turn_first

~ turn_first
adela_druskenvald [smile]: First up is you, darling, with the look of a person who has lost something and isn't sure what.
adela_druskenvald [neutral]: Let's see what the road ahead is keeping warm for you.
reading read hero_1 adela_druskenvald
adela_druskenvald [smile]: Oh, isn't that the bee's knees! That card practically jumped into your lap.
-> turn_second

~ turn_second
adela_druskenvald [smile]: Now for you, with your shoulders squared like you're waiting for the sky to drop.
adela_druskenvald [sly]: Don't fret, the cards are terribly fond of the stubborn ones.
reading read hero_2 adela_druskenvald
adela_druskenvald [neutral]: Well now, that's a deep one to draw on a moving train.
-> turn_third

~ turn_third
adela_druskenvald [neutral]: And you there, watching the corners of the room like you've already counted the doors.
adela_druskenvald [smile]: Hold still a breath, darling, this one wants to turn itself.
reading read hero_3 adela_druskenvald
adela_druskenvald [sly]: Don't look so innocent, darling, the deck knows your sort by heart.
-> turn_fourth

~ turn_fourth
adela_druskenvald [smile]: Last of the four, and saving a mighty quiet pair of eyes for the end.
adela_druskenvald [neutral]: One more turn of the pasteboard, darling, and the set is whole.
reading read hero_4 adela_druskenvald
adela_druskenvald [smile]: My word, you don't do things by halves, do you?
-> reactions

# The cards that touch her: she covers every one of them within half a breath.
~ reactions
if flag.tarot_hero_1 == "the_lovers" or flag.tarot_hero_2 == "the_lovers" or flag.tarot_hero_3 == "the_lovers" or flag.tarot_hero_4 == "the_lovers"
adela_druskenvald [neutral]: Oh. Well now.
adela_druskenvald [sad]: It's funny how they pair you up, isn't it, Philly, even when the road gets dark.
adela_druskenvald [smile]: Oh, that one's got my name on it, near enough.
Narrator: Her smile is bright as a new coin, though her fingers have gone white on the card's soft edge.
endif
if flag.tarot_hero_1 == "the_devil" or flag.tarot_hero_2 == "the_devil" or flag.tarot_hero_3 == "the_devil" or flag.tarot_hero_4 == "the_devil"
adela_druskenvald [sly]: Well, look at the horns on him, darling, he almost matches Philly's walking stick.
adela_druskenvald [neutral]: Pay the grin no mind, it only means the bargain's got teeth in it.
endif
if flag.tarot_hero_1 == "death" or flag.tarot_hero_2 == "death" or flag.tarot_hero_3 == "death" or flag.tarot_hero_4 == "death"
adela_druskenvald [afraid]: It never means what it sounds like, darling.
adela_druskenvald [neutral]: Just a door shutting behind you, that's all it ever is, a clean sweep and a new coat.
adela_druskenvald [smile]: Honestly, it's a swell card once you get past the bones!
endif
if flag.tarot_hero_1 == "the_tower" or flag.tarot_hero_2 == "the_tower" or flag.tarot_hero_3 == "the_tower" or flag.tarot_hero_4 == "the_tower"
adela_druskenvald [neutral]: Stone coming down, a lick of fire in the rafters, and a very good view on the way to the ground.
adela_druskenvald [weary]: Now why on earth did I put it like that?
endif
if flag.tarot_hero_1 == "the_fool" or flag.tarot_hero_2 == "the_fool" or flag.tarot_hero_3 == "the_fool" or flag.tarot_hero_4 == "the_fool"
adela_druskenvald [smile]: Oh, you lucky thing, that's the best card in the deck, it means a beginning!
adela_druskenvald [sly]: Your prize isn't even far, darling, it's waiting right where the road ends in mud.
endif
if flag.tarot_hero_1 == "the_world" or flag.tarot_hero_2 == "the_world" or flag.tarot_hero_3 == "the_world" or flag.tarot_hero_4 == "the_world"
adela_druskenvald [smile]: Look at that, the last card in the deck and the very first in the book!
adela_druskenvald [sly]: Somebody here is going to get what they wished for. And I do hope it's a nice wish.
endif
if flag.tarot_hero_1 == "the_star" or flag.tarot_hero_1 == "the_moon" or flag.tarot_hero_1 == "the_sun" or flag.tarot_hero_2 == "the_star" or flag.tarot_hero_2 == "the_moon" or flag.tarot_hero_2 == "the_sun" or flag.tarot_hero_3 == "the_star" or flag.tarot_hero_3 == "the_moon" or flag.tarot_hero_3 == "the_sun" or flag.tarot_hero_4 == "the_star" or flag.tarot_hero_4 == "the_moon" or flag.tarot_hero_4 == "the_sun"
adela_druskenvald [smile]: Now those three up above aren't iron or gold you can pocket, darling, they're gifts.
adela_druskenvald [neutral]: The sky's own presents, and they'll find you when you look up at the right hour.
endif
-> finish

~ finish
set tarot_full_reading
adela_druskenvald [smile]: There now, all done and dusted, and I think you're all swell!
adela_druskenvald [neutral]: Do you feel that little hum in your fingers? That's the cards settling in to keep you company.
adela_druskenvald [sly]: Don't tell anyone what the cards said. You will, of course. Everyone does.
phillip_druskenvald [neutral]: I have a rule never to have my fortune told. I find it spoils the surprise.
phillip_druskenvald [smile]: Still, if my darling says the road has gifts for you, I wouldn't bet a nickel against her.
Narrator: A quiet warmth settles over your shoulders like a borrowed coat, smelled of cedar and old parlour smoke.
if flag.gl_crashed
-> ghostlight_express/druskenvalds_wreck:reflect_router
endif
-> ghostlight_express/druskenvalds_lounge:menu

~ ask_again
adela_druskenvald [neutral]: Oh, I couldn't possibly pull them a second time, darling, the cards have said what they came to say.
adela_druskenvald [sly]: You can't ask them twice on the same trip, you know, they sulk.
if flag.gl_crashed
-> ghostlight_express/druskenvalds_wreck:menu
endif
-> ghostlight_express/druskenvalds_lounge:menu
